Files Transfer for Herdr

This product is a modified version of File Icons for Herdr
(https://github.com/amster93/herdr-file-icons, Apache-2.0), which is itself
modified from the Herdr app's shipped `files` mod
(https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr-app, Apache-2.0).

Changes in Files Transfer: a right-click menu on files and folders (download to
~/Downloads, paste/upload from Finder, copy path, reveal in Finder, new file,
new folder, rename, move to Trash, delete with confirmation), Markdown and
image previews, a hand-off to Preview Plus when paired, drag-and-drop upload, background transfers over scp for remote
machines, English and Russian interface text, the install script, and the
mod's renaming to files-transfer.

Icons in mods/files-transfer/icons/ come from Material Icon Theme
(https://github.com/material-extensions/vscode-material-icon-theme), MIT.
Menu and chevron glyphs come from Lucide (https://lucide.dev), ISC.
finder.svg and spinner.svg are copied from the Herdr app's workspace-chrome
mod (Apache-2.0).

Windows adaptation (2026-11-17): Windows Explorer clipboard/paste and Ctrl+V,
Explorer reveal, Recycle Bin, native PowerShell filesystem operations, detached
Windows transfers, atomic no-overwrite publication, remote Windows filesystem
helper, normalized paths, Windows image metadata, and a non-overwriting Windows
installer that clones the active layout. The module is named files-transfer-windows.
Original source: https://github.com/vladimiryakimenko/herdr-files-transfer
Upstream baseline: 28f84ddd0b72704011740a428cf722ddf455648c.
Original copyrights, LICENSE and third-party license files are retained.

Explorer additions (2026-11-17): folder entry/back/up navigation, terminal-folder reset, refresh toolbar, modification timestamps and persistent name/date ordering.

Follow-mode additions (2026-11-17): default-on terminal tracking, explicit ON/OFF toolbar state, manual-navigation pinning of folder and machine, and tracking resumption.

Files workflow additions: editable folder paths, name filters, file sizes, multi-selection,
opening a terminal from Files, local/remote split view, and Windows transfer progress,
cancellation, retry and saved download destinations.
